    "title": "Lions men's golf concludes play at the Bulldog Classic",
    "text": "The Purdue Northwest Lions men's golf team returned to action Monday and Tuesday at The Bulldog Classic, hosted by Ferris State at Katke Golf Course in Big Rapids, Michigan. The Lions competed across three rounds against a field featuring several regional opponents.\nThe basics\n- Event: The Bulldog Classic\n- Location: Katke GC – Big Rapids, Michigan\n- Host: Ferris State University\nThe players\nConnor O'Malley(River Falls, Wis./River Falls) – led the Lions with a three-round total of 228 (75-76-77), finishing tied for 31st.Maxwell Abel(Valparaiso, Ind./Valparaiso) – finished tied for 35th with a 231 (75-80-76).William Donovan(Noblesville, Ind./Argyle) – carded a 235 (79-79-77) to finish 44th.Harrison Odle(Rensselaer, Ind./Rensselaer Central) – posted a 238 (81-79-78), tying for 48th.Joshua Gareth Hamilton(Johannesburg, Gauteng/Abbey Park) – closed out the tournament with a 238 (76-85-77), finishing 55th.\nUp next\nThe Lions will continue their fall schedule at the Crossroads Cup on September 28 in Nashport, Ohio, at The Virtues golf course.",
